      "content": "Answer the following question with a single MySQL SQL query against the current database. Explore the semantic network and verify with mysql_query as needed. The SELECT list must contain exactly the columns the question asks for, in the asked order. When the final SQL is verified, call the submit_SQL tool with it.\n\nThe following hints are provided to help you write the SQL:\n\n## Gold Tables\n- SIS_DEPARTMENT\n- MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY\n- LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED\n- TIP_DETAIL\n- SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY\n\n## Column Mapping\n- student full name: MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.FULL_NAME\n- email address: MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.EMAIL_ADDRESS\n- department full name: SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_FULL_NAME\n- department is degree-granting: SIS_DEPARTMENT.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING\n- student year: MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.STUDENT_YEAR\n- difference between length of full name and average length: MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.FULL_NAME\n- school name: LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_SCHOOL_NAME\n- minimum number of enrolled students: LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n- total number of units: SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS\n- department code: SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE, LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_CODE\n- required material: TIP_DETAIL.TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY\n\n## Join Keys\n- MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT <-> SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\n- LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ID <-> TIP_DETAIL.SUBJECT_ID\n- SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_ID <-> TIP_DETAIL.SUBJECT_ID\n\n## Subquery Decomposition\n1. For students whose department is degree-granting and whose student year is 'G', show their full name, email address, department full name, and assign row numbers within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by the student's full name.\n```sql\nSELECT t1.FULL_NAME, t1.EMAIL_ADDRESS, t0.DEPARTMENT_FULL_NAME, ROW_NUMBER() OVER (ORDER BY t1.FULL_NAME ROWS BETWEEN 2 PRECEDING AND 1 FOLLOWING) AS window_column FROM SIS_DEPARTMENT t0 JOIN MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY t1 ON t0.DEPARTMENT_CODE = t1.DEPARTMENT WHERE t0.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y' AND t1.STUDENT_YEAR = 'G'\n```\n2. What is the minimum number of enrolled students in the library subject offerings and the total number of units for subjects that have at least one required material and are offered by the Engineering school?\n```sql\nSELECT MIN(lso.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) AS min_enrolled_students, SUM(sos.TOTAL_UNITS) AS total_units FROM LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED lso JOIN TIP_DETAIL td ON lso.SUBJECT_ID = td.SUBJECT_ID JOIN SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY sos ON td.SUBJECT_ID = sos.SUBJECT_ID WHERE td.TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY = 'RQ' AND lso.OFFER_SCHOOL_NAME = 'Engineering';\n```\n3. For students whose department is degree-granting and whose student year is 'G', show their full name, email address, department full name, and the difference between the length of their full name and the average length of full names for all such students.\n```sql\nWITH inner_cte AS ( SELECT t1.FULL_NAME, t1.EMAIL_ADDRESS, t0.DEPARTMENT_FULL_NAME FROM SIS_DEPARTMENT t0 JOIN MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY t1 ON t0.DEPARTMENT_CODE = t1.DEPARTMENT WHERE t0.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y' AND t1.STUDENT_YEAR = 'G' ) SELECT i.FULL_NAME, i.EMAIL_ADDRESS, i.DEPARTMENT_FULL_NAME, (LENGTH(i.FULL_NAME) - avg_len.avg_full_name_length) AS diff_from_avg_length FROM inner_cte i JOIN ( SELECT AVG(LENGTH(FULL_NAME)) AS avg_full_name_length FROM inner_cte ) avg_len ON 1=1;\n```\n4. For each school, what is the minimum number of enrolled students in the library subject offerings and the total number of units for subjects that have at least one required material? For each school, also include a grand total for all such subjects in the format of (school, null, total units, min enrolled students).\n```sql\nWITH inner_cte AS ( SELECT lso.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS, sos.TOTAL_UNITS, lso.OFFER_SCHOOL_NAME FROM LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED lso JOIN TIP_DETAIL td ON lso.SUBJECT_ID = td.SUBJECT_ID JOIN SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY sos ON td.SUBJECT_ID = sos.SUBJECT_ID WHERE td.TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY = 'RQ' ) SELECT OFFER_SCHOOL_NAME, MIN(NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) AS min_enrolled_students, SUM(TOTAL_UNITS) AS total_units FROM inner_cte GROUP BY OFFER_SCHOOL_NAME WITH ROLLUP HAVING SUM(TOTAL_UNITS) > 0 ORDER BY OFFER_SCHOOL_NAME\n```\n\n## Question\nFor each student whose department is degree-granting and whose student year is 'G', show their full name, email address, department full name, and the difference between the length of their full name and the average length of full names for all such students. For each such student, also show, for each school in which their department offers subjects with at least one required material, the school name, the minimum number of enrolled students in those library subject offerings, and the total number of units for those subjects. Do not return any rounded answers."
