      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The database connection is persistently failing with an authentication error (`Access denied for user 'root'@'localhost'`), so direct data verification is not possible. I'll complete the investigation using the semantic network evidence and the provided hints, then construct the SQL carefully.\n\n---\n\n# Investigation Report\n\n## 1. Entity Semantics\n\n**Tables (all retrieved via `semantic_get`):**\n\n- **SIS_DEPARTMENT** — SIS department dimension, one row per academic department. Key columns: `DEPARTMENT_CODE` (joins to offering tables and `MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT`), `DEPARTMENT_FULL_NAME` (\"Full official name of the department\"), `IS_DEGREE_GRANTING` (\"'Y'/'N' flag whether the department is degree granting\"), `SCHOOL_NAME`.\n- **MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY** — one row per student. Key columns: `FULL_NAME` (\"Full name in 'Last, First M.' format\"), `EMAIL_ADDRESS`, `DEPARTMENT` (\"Academic department code the student belongs to; joins to SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\"), `STUDENT_YEAR` (\"e.g. 'G' for graduate\").\n- **LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED** — one row per subject per term in library reserve scope. Key columns: `SUBJECT_ID` (\"joins to TIP_DETAIL.SUBJECT_ID\"), `OFFER_DEPT_CODE` (\"Offering department code\"), `OFFER_SCHOOL_NAME` (\"Offering school name\"), `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS` (\"Number of students enrolled in the subject per library records\").\n- **TIP_DETAIL** — one row per subject-material-status combination per term. Key columns: `SUBJECT_ID`, `TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY` (\"'RQ' = Required\" per TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS decode).\n- **SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY** — one row per subject per term (registrar rollup). Key columns: `SUBJECT_ID` (\"joins to TIP_DETAIL.SUBJECT_ID and LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ID\"), `TOTAL_UNITS` (\"Total credit units of the subject\").\n\n**Column concepts:**\n- `column_concept_subject_id` — SUBJECT_ID is the cross-domain subject join key ('CODE.NUMBER' format) across TIP, library, and registrar tables; decision guide: \"Joining textbook materials or library reserves to catalog/summary subject attributes → Match on SUBJECT_ID\".\n- `column_concept_material_status_key` — decision guide: \"Questions about required or optional textbooks → Filter TIP_DETAIL.TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY … 'RQ' for required only.\"\n- `column_concept_total_units` — decision guide: \"Unit statistics at subject-offering rollup level with offering department/school → Use SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS.\"\n- `column_concept_enrollment_measures` — decision guide: \"Questions about enrollment of subjects within … library reserve scope → Use … LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS.\"\n\n**Concepts:**\n- `concept_department_dimension` — decision guide: \"Questions filtering departments by school … or degree-granting status → Use SIS_DEPARTMENT; it carries SCHOOL_NAME and IS_DEGREE_GRANTING.\"\n- `concept_course_material_programs` — TIP and library reserve programs \"linked by SUBJECT_ID + TERM_CODE\"; required-textbook questions use TIP_DETAIL with status 'RQ'.\n\n## 2. Lineage & Relationships\n\nFrom `semantic_graph` on LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED and TIP_DETAIL:\n- LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED ↔ TIP_DETAIL: documented `joins` edge (both directions retrieved), on SUBJECT_ID.\n- LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED ↔ SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY: documented `joins` edge, on SUBJECT_ID.\n- LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED → SIS_DEPARTMENT: documented `joins` edge (OFFER_DEPT_CODE = DEPARTMENT_CODE).\n- MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT → SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE: stated in both table descriptions.\n- Both fact tables belong to `concept_subject_offering_facts` and `concept_course_material_programs`; SIS_DEPARTMENT belongs to `concept_department_dimension`; MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY belongs to `concept_person_directory`.\n\n## 3. Similar-Entity Differences\n\n**3a. Dimension matrix (candidates for each task requirement):**\n\n| Requirement | Candidate | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| Degree-granting flag | SIS_DEPARTMENT.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING (SUPPORTED — only table with the flag; STUDENT_DEPARTMENT has \"no degree-granting flag\" per concept comparison) | concept_department_dimension comparisons |\n| Department full name | SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_FULL_NAME (SUPPORTED); STUDENT_DEPARTMENT also has full name but lacks the flag, so SIS_DEPARTMENT is the single-table solution | concept comparison \"Attribute coverage\" |\n| Student name/email/year | MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.FULL_NAME / EMAIL_ADDRESS / STUDENT_YEAR (SUPPORTED — only student table with these; SE_PERSON has no email) | table columns |\n| School name of offering | LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_SCHOOL_NAME (SUPPORTED); SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.OFFER_SCHOOL_NAME also exists, but the question says \"library subject offerings\" for the enrollment measure, anchoring the offering-side table to LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED | column defs; hint mapping |\n| Min enrolled students | LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS (SUPPORTED — \"library subject offerings\" wording); SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS is registrar-scope, not library | column_concept_enrollment_measures |\n| Total units | SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS (SUPPORTED — LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED has NO units column at all, verified in retrieved columns) | SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY columns |\n| Required material | TIP_DETAIL.TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY = 'RQ' (SUPPORTED — 'RQ' = Required); library's own status 'Y' = Required Course Material is a different domain and the hints/gold tables anchor to TIP | column_concept_material_status_key |\n\n**3b. Task-Requirement Fitness Mapping:** All five gold tables are SUPPORTED for their mapped requirements; no candidate violates any requirement. LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED lacks TOTAL_UNITS (objective), hence the SUBJECT_ID join to SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY is mandatory.\n\n**3c. Wording-to-Field Anchoring:**\n- \"department is degree-granting\" → `SIS_DEPARTMENT.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y'`.\n- \"student year is 'G'\" → `MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.STUDENT_YEAR = 'G'`.\n- \"at least one required material\" → `TIP_DETAIL.TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY = 'RQ'` (decision guide: \"'RQ' for required only\").\n- \"minimum number of enrolled students in those **library subject offerings**\" → `MIN(LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS)`.\n- \"total number of units\" → `SUM(SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS)`.\n- \"each school in which **their department** offers subjects\" → group by (`LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_CODE`, `OFFER_SCHOOL_NAME`) and match `OFFER_DEPT_CODE` to the student's department code — the hint's Join-Key list explicitly pairs `SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE` with `LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_CODE`.\n- \"average length of full names for **all such students**\" → average over the student population (degree-granting + 'G'), i.e., the inner student CTE — matching hint subquery 3, not over the student×school joined rows.\n\n**3d. Precedent Usage Evidence:** Hint subquery 2/4 precedent: `LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED JOIN TIP_DETAIL ON SUBJECT_ID JOIN SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY ON SUBJECT_ID WHERE TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY='RQ'` with `MIN(NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS)` and `SUM(TOTAL_UNITS)` — exactly the same task shape (2 precedents given). Hint subquery 3 precedent: CTE + cross-joined `AVG(LENGTH(FULL_NAME))` for the difference-from-average pattern. Multiple metrics (dw_3398, dw_2180, dw_4724) use the same TIP 'RQ' + SUBJECT_ID join pattern.\n\n## 4. Business Usage\n\n- SIS_DEPARTMENT: consumed by dozens of metrics for degree-granting/school filters (dw_1033, dw_3237, dw_1350, etc.).\n- MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY: used for graduate-student ('G') population questions (dw_100, dw_1212, dw_1033).\n- LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED + TIP_DETAIL + SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY: standard trio for \"subjects with required materials, library enrollment, registrar units\" questions (dw_3398, dw_2180, dw_4724, dw_3911).\n\n## 5. Coverage Checklist\n\n- SIS_DEPARTMENT, MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY, LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED, TIP_DETAIL, SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY — `semantic_get` ✓, `semantic_graph` (LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED, TIP_DETAIL) ✓.\n- concept_department_dimension, concept_course_material_programs — `semantic_get` ✓.\n- column_concept_subject_id, column_concept_material_status_key, column_concept_total_units, column_concept_enrollment_measures — `semantic_get` ✓.\n- Other Phase-1 hits (EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY, SE_PERSON, TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED, SUBJECT_SUMMARY, LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL, STUDENT_DEPARTMENT, etc.) — screened via retrieved descriptions/column comparisons; none carries a required column absent from the five gold tables (STUDENT_DEPARTMENT lacks IS_DEGREE_GRANTING; TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED is program-scope enrollment, not \"library subject offerings\"; SUBJECT_SUMMARY is not in the hint join path). `mysql_query` verification was attempted 5 times but the database rejected all connections (access denied), so no data-level checks could be run.\n\n## 6. Recommendation\n\n**6a. Tables/columns:** the five gold tables exactly as mapped above — measure columns `LENGTH(FULL_NAME) − AVG(LENGTH(FULL_NAME))` (over the student CTE), `MIN(LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS)`, `SUM(SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS)`; keys `MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT = SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE`, `LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_CODE = student's department code`, `SUBJECT_ID` chain across the three offering/material tables; filters `IS_DEGREE_GRANTING='Y'`, `STUDENT_YEAR='G'`, `TIP_MATERIAL_STATUS_KEY='RQ'`.\n\n**6b. SQL approach:** CTE 1 = qualifying students (with department code retained for the school join); scalar average of `LENGTH(FULL_NAME)` over CTE 1 (per hint subquery 3, so the average is over students, not joined rows); CTE 2 = per (OFFER_DEPT_CODE, OFFER_SCHOOL_NAME) aggregation of the RQ-material join chain (per hint subqueries 2/4, joining on SUBJECT_ID only); final INNER JOIN of students to CTE 2 on department code, cross join to the average. No rounding applied. Caveat: the SUBJECT_ID-only join (no TERM_CODE) fans out across terms — this is the documented precedent pattern in the hints, and MIN/SUM are computed over that joined population as in precedents dw_3398-style queries.\n\n**6c. Three-perspective reasons:**\n- **Data**: LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED physically lacks any units column (verified in retrieved columns), so SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS via SUBJECT_ID is the only source; MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY is the only table with student FULL_NAME+EMAIL_ADDRESS+STUDENT_YEAR+academic DEPARTMENT code.\n- **Semantic-network**: documented `joins` edges LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED↔TIP_DETAIL↔SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY on SUBJECT_ID; decision guides anchor 'RQ'=required, library-scope enrollment, and IS_DEGREE_GRANTING to SIS_DEPARTMENT.\n- **Business**: hint subqueries 2/3/4 are direct precedents for both halves of this compound question; numerous dw_ metrics use the identical RQ + SUBJECT_ID join shape.\n\n**6d. Alternatives:** pre-aggregating per (dept, school) vs. row-level join + GROUP BY per (student, school) produce identical values; I use the pre-aggregated form for clarity. LEFT vs INNER join for students whose department has no RQ-material subjects: the question's phrasing (\"for each school in which their department offers…\") and the hint precedents (plain JOINs) support INNER JOIN.\n\nFinal SQL:\n\n",
